    - target: {fileID: 6380436179282662226, guid: 76354cb641cf5aa46ba4902d9b7024f7, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "<font=\"bold\">Haarlem </font>railway station is located in Haarlem
        in North Holland, Netherlands. The station opened at September 20, 1839,
        on the Amsterdam\u2013Rotterdam railway, the first railway line in the Netherlands.
        The station building itself is a rijksmonument. \nThe original, wooden station
        was built on the Oude Weg, just outside the Amsterdamse Poort in 1839 to
        accommodate the passengers of the first railway in the Netherlands between
        Haarlem and Amsterdam. The station was built outside the city, on the current
        location of the Centrale Werkplaats (maintenance depot) of the Hollandsche
        IJzeren Spoorweg-Maatschappij. "
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
